<Skein rootNode="node-179">
  <generator>Windows Inform 10.1.2</generator>
  <item nodeId="node-179">
    <command xml:space="preserve">SoMe-Universe-IF</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">SoMe-Universe: The Ten Banners&#x000A;Ten powers want you. Decide who to become. by The SoMe-Universe Contributors&#x000A;Release 1 / Serial number 260923 / Inform 7 v10.1.2 / D&#x000A;&#x000A;Singularity&#x000A;You are in the Singularity. The universe is beginning to explode.&#x000A;&#x000A;Three roads leave the newborn light: the Hall of Medicine to the south, the Disease Citadel to the north - and a third way, west, where the land glows wrong. The Ten wait behind them for the first traveler to walk the war. The west road belongs to the Old Metals, and the stories agree: look, but do not look like food.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-180"/>
      <child nodeId="node-222"/>
      <child nodeId="node-223"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-180">
    <command xml:space="preserve">n</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have walked into the Unseen Crown's domain. Six banners crown the dark hall, and under each waits a recruiter who wants your oath:&#x000A;&#x000A;   a plain-clothes veteran Archaea (the Archaeology Division), a containment supervisor with a drone on her shoulder (Fear Technology), a sunflower muse (the Pale Masquerade), a pale Bride of Count Dracula (the Undead Court), a personnel officer (the Department of Silence), and a gum-chewing girl in a sailor suit (the Abyssal Legion).&#x000A;&#x000A;Court any of them before you swear - each hides a secret, if you ask. When one wins you over: CHOOSE VIBRIO, CHOOSE DRACULA, CHOOSE FEAR, CHOOSE ARCHAEOLOGY, CHOOSE PALLIDUM, or CHOOSE STILLE. For example: ASK THE GIRL ABOUT JOINING.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-181"/>
      <child nodeId="node-182"/>
      <child nodeId="node-191"/>
      <child nodeId="node-192"/>
      <child nodeId="node-193"/>
      <child nodeId="node-195"/>
      <child nodeId="node-196"/>
      <child nodeId="node-201"/>
      <child nodeId="node-207"/>
      <child nodeId="node-218"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-181">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask archaeologist about joining</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(the Archaeology Recruiter about that)&#x000A;The archaeologist thumbs her steaming probe. "Archaea are the original Umin. We are not inventing, envoy - we are remembering. Join the Division and dig where the war was first invented: the vents, the salt, the anaerobic dark."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-182">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask bride about joining</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The Bride smiles, and does not trouble to hide the teeth. "Straight talk, envoy, since everyone else here is ciphering. We are vampires. Real ones: the disease is rabies, the folklore was a warning, and our sovereign is Count Dracula - the Count to you, once you are family. Join the Court and you stop aging, stop fearing the dark, and start belonging to something that has outlived every empire that ever banned it. The recruitment terms are simple: one bite. The benefits are eternal. The Catch-22 is that you have to die a little first. Most of our best people did."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-183"/>
      <child nodeId="node-185"/>
      <child nodeId="node-189"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-183">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask bride about light</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">She counts the Court's three fears on white fingers. "Sunlight - it will kill me, not inconvenience me; the folklore undersold it. Running water - the old rivers still remember the old law. And the bite - which is not fear at all, envoy, but the front door. Everything else your species dreads is a variation with worse press."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-184"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-184">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask bride about water</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">She counts the Court's three fears on white fingers. "Sunlight - it will kill me, not inconvenience me; the folklore undersold it. Running water - the old rivers still remember the old law. And the bite - which is not fear at all, envoy, but the front door. Everything else your species dreads is a variation with worse press."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-185">
    <command xml:space="preserve">choose Undead Court</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The Count regards you across the dry fountains. "Fear is not a weapon. Fear is the battlefield," he says. "Welcome to the field." You swear to the Undead Court.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;The war arranges itself around your oath. Somewhere on neutral waters, a Registrar adds a name to a ledger and begins cataloguing the conflict: the Ten Banners campaign.&#x000A;An Accord manifest appears in your satchel.&#x000A;(Type BANNERS at any time to review the campaign.)&#x000A;&#x000A;The Singularity seals itself behind the Big Bang. The gates open. A launch skiff carries you to neutral waters.&#x000A;&#x000A;The circuit of the Ten Banners begins.&#x000A;&#x000A;Free Port Landing&#x000A;The landing stage of the Pericardium Free Port, the one place the war may not touch: tariffs fund the Cradle, every flag may dock, and no act of war may be committed within the pericardial sac. The Registrar keeps the standards here, under Accord charter, where every faction's oath-binding is neutral ground. Go to any banner's hall from this deck - the port's manifests know them all.&#x000A;&#x000A;On the chart table is a Rationality Protocol pamphlet.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Registrar stands by the ten standards with a ledger under one arm, cataloguing the war before it happens, on neutral ground no faction dare violate.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;HOW TO TRAVEL: no compass needed at this hub. List every destination:&#x000A;      ASK REGISTRAR ABOUT DESTINATIONS&#x000A;then jump straight there:&#x000A;      GO TO UNDEAD COURT      or      GO TO MARKET      (GO TO LANDING brings you home.)&#x000A;Carry every won seal home and REPORT to raise the standards.&#x000A;&#x000A;HOW TO WALK: directions still work where roads exist - type N / S / and so on to walk a real road instead of using the concordance.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-186"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-186">
    <command xml:space="preserve">go to undead court</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The manifest takes your word, and the concordance carries you along the great vessels of the war.&#x000A;&#x000A;Blood Court&#x000A;The court of the Undead: a long dry hall where fountains stand as architecture only, running nothing. Dracula holds the far end like a fixed point the room is measured from. Three Brides flank him - Budapest, Bucharest, Belgrade - and the gallery behind is walled in glass, with what is preserved in the glass better left undescribed. Every surface is dark, dry, and exactly 0.1 lux.&#x000A;&#x000A;Count Dracula stands at the far end of the dry hall. He does not so much hold the room as permit it to continue.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Budapest Bride watches the stair, unhurried.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Bucharest Bride stands where the gallery light ends, which is a professional habit.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Belgrade Bride has a physician's hands, and the file on her is the thinnest.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-187"/>
    </children>
  </item>
